#!RuleTest
#test CT-RUN-1 expect=noViolation domain=VS
#note Fold F1 pin of TODAY's output — an ADaM run never reads a Trial Summary (CTD-2: ADaM has no TS, define only). Its define declares only define-xmlct, a root ADaM never consumes, so the run stays on the define (step 4), names nothing, and the CT rule finds no library codelist and does not fire — with no note. The TS names sdtmct-1999-01-01, which the store lacks: a wrongful TS read would name it and ABORT.
#run-product adam/adamig-1-3
#define-xml define-21-define-xmlct-only.xml
#ct-available none
dataset VS
col VSSTAT type=Char
---
BOGUS
---

dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSVCDREF type=Char
col TSVCDVER type=Char
---
S1 | TCNTRL | PLACEBO | CDISC CT | 1999-01-01
